# Web design quality

Fits **Harness** expectations: **`planner`** Design direction + **`frontend-evaluator`** “anti-ai-slop” scoring.

## Anti-template

Avoid shipping **generic SaaS-placeholder** layouts: unmotivated centered hero + gradient blob, identical card grids, default library skin with no tailoring, gray-on-gray timidity everywhere.

### Push for (pick a direction deliberately)

Strong **hierarchy**, **spacing rhythm**, **layering/motion**, **paired typography**, **semantic color**, designed **interaction states**, intentional **layouts** (bento / editorial / scrolly where spec calls for it).

## Before implementing UI

1. Concrete visual direction (**not** only “minimal / modern”).
2. Named palette + type roles.
3. A few **real references** (products, comps art-direction).
4. Align with **`docs/project/project.md`** and the issue spec when the harness is active.

## Component checklist

- [ ] Avoids looking like untouched Tailwind / shadcn demo
- [ ] Hover / focus / active / disabled feel intentional
- [ ] Hierarchy: not everything same weight/size
- [ ] Readable in plausible product screenshot — matches **frontend-evaluator** bar